description:
CONFIRMED by an adversarial reviewer during PR #140 (LCLI-467).

backlogRemovalReadiness asks git two questions. It never runs planBacklogSnapshot, which refuses ANY symlink segment or non-regular entry under backlog/. Git tracks symlinks natively and reports them clean, so readiness says ready:true for a state archiveAndDeleteBacklog then refuses:

  backlog/tasks/note.md -> ../../shared/note.md   (committed, clean)
  readiness -> {"ready":true}
  archiveAndDeleteBacklog -> LoreError "drift": refusing to archive through symlink

CONSEQUENCES, read from the call site (no catch around offerBacklogRemoval, only finally{prompter.close()}):
 - the operator is asked a destructive question that CANNOT succeed;
 - answering yes aborts the whole `lore init` with exit 6 (drift), not the exit 4 the new docs promise for a refused removal;
 - persistTrackerBackend and the migration have already run, but the agents/codex bridges and the scaffolds -- questions the operator already answered -- never run, and no init envelope is emitted;
 - backlog/ is untouched (the leg is failure-atomic), so there is NO data loss;
 - the hint says "rerun the cutover", vocabulary from --adopt-manifest that is meaningless on the plain-migration path. That copy defect is newly REACHABLE because of LCLI-467.

TWO FIXES, either acceptable: have offerBacklogRemoval / resolveScriptedBacklogRemoval wrap the call and downgrade a drift refusal to a reported non-removal (removed:false, reason) instead of aborting the run; or extend readiness to run planBacklogSnapshot (read-only) and fold its refusal into ready:false with a reason. The second makes the gate and the archive agree, which is also what LCLI-521's sibling finding wants.

CARRY INTO LCLI-519: this shows the wizard's write-ordering invariant now degrades differently -- a crash at the archive step leaves the tracker persisted, the migration applied, and the operator's agent/scaffold answers unapplied.
